# Simple two-plane right-angle chute (floor + wall)
# Axis convention matches ChutePoseAnalysis.m's local chute frame exactly:
#   X = slide/length axis   (roll rotates about this axis; floor+wall share this span)
#   Y = floor-recede axis   (floor occupies Y<=0; wall seam at Y=0; pitch rotates about this axis)
#   Z = wall-height axis    (floor at Z=0; wall rises Z>=0)
# length=1.0 (X)  depth=0.6 (Y)  height=0.6 (Z)
v -16.00000 -8.0000 0.000000
v -16.00000 0.000000 0.000000
v 16.00000 0.000000 0.000000
v 16.00000 -8.0000 0.000000
v -16.00000 0.000000 0.000000
v -16.00000 0.000000 8.0000
v 16.00000 0.000000 8.0000
v 16.00000 0.000000 0.000000

f 1 3 2
f 1 4 3
f 5 7 6
f 5 8 7
f 3 4 7
